 "14", "title": "The curse of border vacuums,", "pagenum": "257", "type": {"key": "/type/toc_item"}}, {"level": 0, "label": "15", "title": "Unslumming and slumming,", "pagenum": "270", "type": {"key": "/type/toc_item"}}, {"level": 0, "label": "16", "title": "Gradual money and cataclysmic money,", "pagenum": "291", "type": {"key": "/type/toc_item"}}, {"level": 0, "title": "DIFFERENT TACTICS", "type": {"key": "/type/toc_item"}}, {"level": 0, "label": "17", "title": "Subsidizing dwellings,", "pagenum": "321", "type": {"key": "/type/toc_item"}}, {"level": 0, "label": "18", "title": "Erosion of cities or attrition of automobiles,", "pagenum": "338", "type": {"key": "/type/toc_item"}}, {"level": 0, "label": "19", "title": "Visual order: its limitations and possibilities,", "pagenum": "372", "type": {"key": "/type/toc_item"}}, {"level": 0, "label": "20", "title": "Salvaging projects,", "pagenum": "392", "type": {"key": "/type/toc_item"}}, {"level": 0, "label": "21", "title": "Governing and planning districts,", "pagenum": "405", "type": {"key": "/type/toc_item"}}, {"level": 0, "label": "22", "title": "The kind of problem a city is,", "pagenum": "428", "type": {"key": "/type/toc_item"}}, {"level": 0, "title": "Index", "pagenum": "449", "type": {"key": "/type/toc_item"}}], "description": "A direct and fundamentally optimistic indictment of the short-sightedness and intellectual arrogance that has characterized much of urban planning in this century, The Death and Life of Great American Cities has, since its first publication in 1961, become the standard against which all endeavors in that field are measured. In prose of outstanding immediacy, Jane Jacobs writes about what makes streets safe or unsafe; about what constitutes a neighborhood, and what function it serves within the larger organism of the city; about why some neighborhoods remain impoverished while others regenerate themselves. She writes about the salutary role of funeral parlors and tenement windows, the dangers of too much development money and too little diversity. Compassionate, bracingly indignant, and always keenly detailed. Jane Jacob's monumental work provides an essential framework for assessing the vitality of cities.", "subject_place": ["United States."], "covers": [420505], "key": "/books/OL1742994M", "authors": [{"key": "/authors/OL29371A"}], "publish_places": ["New York"], "subjects": ["City planning -- United States", "Urban renewal -- United States", "Urban policy -- United States"], "uri_descriptions": ["Contributor biographical information", "Sample text", "Publisher description"], "languages": [{"key": "/languages/eng"}], "pagination": "458 p. :", "source_records": ["marc:marc_records_scriblio_net/part22.dat:183730508:1109", "marc:marc_openlibraries_sanfranciscopubliclibrary/sfpl_chq_2018_12_24_run02.mrc:123607117:2200", "marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC1_barcode.mrc:29043099:4312", "marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part21.utf8:220099764:1114", "marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC1_multibarcode.mrc:29063932:4312", "ia:deathlifeofgreat0000jaco_n0t5", "bwb:9780679741954", "amazon:067974195X", "promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2021-05-14", "idb:9780679741954", "marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-003.mrc:200408405:1552"], "title": "The Death and Life of Great American Cities", "url": ["http://www.loc.gov/catdir/bios/random051/92050082.html", "http://www.loc.gov/catdir/samples/random042/92050082.html", "http://www.loc.gov/catdir/description/random045/92050082.html"], "notes": "Originally published: New York : Random House, [1961].\r\nIncludes index.", "number_of_pages": 458, "edition_name": "Vintage Books ed.", "local_id": ["urn:sfpl:31223087967734", "urn:sfpl:31223087967791", "urn:sfpl:31223087967809", "urn:cst:10011363621", "urn:bwbsku:O7-CIA-694"], "publish_date": "1992", "publish_country": "nyu", "by_statement": "Jane Jacobs.", "works": [{"key": "/works/OL93641W"}], "type": {"key": "/type/edition"}, "uris": ["http://www.loc.gov/catdi